; error: 8:3: task 'zero' is a (flex [int]@r) -> nothing, and wrapper 'logged' takes a ([int]@r) -> nothing first; this task changes what a value it is given reaches, so it goes only where the type says 'flex' for that value, as in '(flex [int]@r) -> nothing', and nothing a fixed name owns is given to it there
; A wrapper takes the task it wraps as that task's type: one changing what its
; slice reaches, '(flex [int]@r) -> nothing'.

task logged(next: ([int]@r) -> nothing, xs: [int]@r)
    next(xs)
fi
$(logged)
